{
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Cell \u2014 MC @ \u03b1=1 brain-only, no DualEMA reward (Goodhart ablation)",
    "description": "Phase v5.1 Goodhart-ablation diagnostic.  Same as the_cell_crossfade_mc_a100.json (MC actor-critic at fixed \u03b1=1 brain-only) but with the reflex_scent_hit DualEMADetector module stripped out.  The only events.hit signal reaching NeurochemState + Premotor is the consummatory on_nutrient_hit fired by the body when an actual nutrient is eaten \u2014 sparse and unbiased.  Diagnostic question: does MC still circle without the gradient-detector reward?  If brain stops circling and random-walks/drifts, MC was Goodharting on the dense anticipatory reward signal.  If brain still circles, the bias is elsewhere (initialisation, MC internals).  Run interactively in the launcher and watch top-down view to compare to the_cell_crossfade_mc_a100 behaviour.",
    "env_target": "cell",
    "phase_tag": "v5.1-goodhart-ablation",
    "reflex_modular": true,
    "body_model": "differential_paddler",
    "episode_length": 3600
  },
  "version": 1,
  "runtime": {
    "thread_pool": "per_instance",
    "num_threads": 0
  },
  "modules": [
